VERDICT (no QED, Clay 0%)
  * f1^2=a0(1 - c u + ...); c = P3 dressed amplitude [R].
  * [T] pin 0<=f1^2<=M0 is exact and SIGN-BLIND (both ends attained by exact models).
  * [T] [R] <-> W differ only by the exact normaliser a0/M0; same obstruction.
  * [NG] KP: the only proven bound |log D_fin|<=Cu needs u*K<1; at 2.5 u*K~1e4.
  * => [R] is NOT boundable at beta=2.5 by expansion/positivity tools:
         it IS the same nonperturbative binding input W.   [O]
